{"name":"Oxblood","hex":"#800020","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"oxblood","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A dark brownish-red colour.","The blood of an ox."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a dark brownish-red colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oxblood"}],"entries":[{"title":"Oxblood","blocks":[{"text":"Oxblood or ox-blood is a dark shade of maroon, and is one of the darkest shades of red. It resembles burgundy, but has less purple and more dark brown hues. The French term sang-de-bœuf, or sang de bœuf, with the same meaning is used in various contexts in English, but especially in pottery, where sang de boeuf glaze in the color is a classic ceramic glaze in Chinese ceramics."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Small_vase_MET_SLP1692-1_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Small_vase_MET_SLP1692-1_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oxblood","wikidata":"Q2013559"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Unlaced_Dr_Martens_Oxblood_Made_in_England_1461_shoes.jpg/500px-Unlaced_Dr_Martens_Oxblood_Made_in_England_1461_shoes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Unlaced_Dr_Martens_Oxblood_Made_in_England_1461_shoes.jpg/1280px-Unlaced_Dr_Martens_Oxblood_Made_in_England_1461_shoes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Unlaced_Dr_Martens_Oxblood_Made_in_England_1461_shoes.jpg/500px-Unlaced_Dr_Martens_Oxblood_Made_in_England_1461_shoes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A pair of oxblood-colour Dr. Martens shoes","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AUnlaced_Dr_Martens_Oxblood_Made_in_England_1461_shoes.jpg"},{"s